---
title: Chocolate Silk Pie
cooklang: 2
servings: 8
cuisine: American
source: recipe-pack desserts-1/8127-chocolate-silk-pie-1
---

= Crust -> crust

`Stir together` @chocolate cookie crumbs{250%g} and @melted butter{115%g} in a #bowl{}. -> crumb mix

`Press` the @&crumb mix{} into a #pie plate{} and up the sides.

= Filling -> filling

`Whisk` @sugar{300%g}, @eggs{4}(room temperature), @cocoa{2%tbsp} and @heavy cream{240%ml} in a
#large saucepan{} until ~{smooth}.

`Cook medium` over medium heat, stirring constantly, until ~{thickened}. -> custard

`Strain` the @&custard{} through a #fine mesh sieve{} into a #large bowl{} and `stir in`
@dark chocolate{200%g}(chopped), @unsalted butter{60%g} and @vanilla extract{1%tsp} until ~{smooth}.
-> chocolate custard

`Cool` to room temperature, ~rest{1-2%hours}, stirring occasionally.

`Whip high` the @&chocolate custard{} on high speed until ~{slightly lightened in colour}, ~{5%minutes}.

`Whip` @&heavy cream{240%ml} in a #+bowl{} until ~{stiff peaks form}. -> whipped cream

`Fold ×2` the @&whipped cream{} into the @&chocolate custard{} in the #&large bowl{} in two batches.

= Assemble

`Spread` the @&filling{} into the @&crust{} in the #&pie plate{} and `chill` ~rest{6%hours} until ~{set}. `Garnish?` with
@?whipped cream{}(sweetened).
